      "clipStartM": 64.43713585376678,
      "clipEndM": 85.42081072006091,
      "derivation": "The framing rule of src/gltf/Framing.h, quoted so the runner can refuse a mismatch rather than trust it. World bounds [-9.165282249450684, -4.332165718078613, -0.5613932993759952] to [9.391292333602905, 5.406499197468161, 0.5000002659955953], so centre = [0.11300504207611084, 0.5371667396947739, -0.03069651669019996] and radius = 10.491837433147069 m. yfov = 2*atan(12/50) from a 50 mm lens on a 24 mm sensor height at sensor_fit VERTICAL. distance = radius / sin(yfov/2) / 0.6 = 74.92897328691384, and the eye is centre + (cos20*cos35, sin20, cos20*sin35) * distance. clipStart is distance - radius and clipEnd is distance + radius.",
      "note": "The glTF carries no camera, so the framing rule supplies one. Roll is 0 because the rule sets it: a roll chosen here and nowhere else would make this subject's placement a second determination competing with the rule."
